        "question_haK74q": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Warranty",
            "answer": "<p>We offer a 250,000 shots or 3-year warranty on nets, whichever comes first. All of our nets have a modular design, so we can quickly and easily provide specific replacement parts necessary to resolve any issues.</p><p>Golf simulator screens are covered for one (1) year from the date of purchase.</p><p><strong>To Obtain Warranty Service:</strong></p><p>Contact us at support@thenetreturn.com.</p><p><em>You will need to provide us with proof of purchase and a description of the defect. We may also ask you to provide photographs or other evidence of the defect. We will then evaluate the claim and determine whether it is covered by this limited warranty.<br/><br/></em><a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/pages/waranty-policy\" title=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/pages/waranty-policy\"><strong>Warranty Policy</strong></a></p>"
          }
        },
        "question_PyjwQW": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Product Usage Guidelines",
            "answer": "<ul><li>Inspect the golf balls you are using and avoid using scuffed or damaged golf ball. These imperfections can cause the ball to act as a knife and can ultimately rip the net.</li><li>Inspect your net for wear and tear such as fraying. We highly recommend you purchase a Net Guardian if your shots are repeatedly hitting the same spot to increase net longevity.</li><li>Avoid leaving the net return outdoors in inclement weather. We also recommend laying our nets down flat during instances of strong winds.</li><li>Ensure your practice area is free and clear of people and objects to prevent injury.</li><li>We recommend pushing excess netting underneath the net towards the back of the frame to ensure proper ball return and reduce premature wear.</li><li>While our <a href=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/collections/bulletproof\" title=\"https://www.thenetreturn.com/collections/bulletproof\">Bulletproof</a> nets are made of DyneemaⓇ and can withstand ball speeds of over 250 mph, they are not bulletproof. Do not attempt to fire a bullet through a Bulletproof net.</li></ul>"
          }
        },
